---
layout: base.njk
title: Copy-Paste PowerShell
description: Plain-English PowerShell for beginners. Commands to copy, safe scripts with -WhatIf, fill-in-the-blank builders, and a bash-to-PowerShell translator.
---
<section class="hero">
  <h1 class="hero-title"><span>Copy-Paste</span> PowerShell</h1>
  <p class="lede">Commands to copy. Scripts that preview before they change anything. Builders that fill in the blanks. Everything explained in plain English.</p>
  <form class="hero-search" role="search" action="/" method="get">
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="home-q">Search</label>
    <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">PS&gt;</span>
    <input id="home-q" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Try: list files, zip, grep, ping" autocomplete="off" data-search-input data-search-primary>
  </form>
  <p class="hero-stats">
    <a href="/commands/"><strong>{{ collections.commands.length }}</strong> commands</a>
    <a href="/scripts/"><strong>{{ collections.scripts.length }}</strong> scripts</a>
    <a href="/builders/"><strong>{{ collections.builders.length }}</strong> builders</a>
    <a href="/guides/"><strong>{{ collections.guides.length }}</strong> guides</a>
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">Start here</p>
    <h2>New to PowerShell?</h2>
    <p>Read these in order. Then skip around.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="guide-steps">
    {% for item in collections.guides %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
        <p>{{ item.data.summary }}</p>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">Cheat sheet</p>
    <h2>Six to learn first</h2>
    <p>These cover most of week one.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="stack">
    {% for item in collections.featuredCommands %}
      <article class="cmd-card">
        <div>
          <a href="{{ item.url }}"><code>{{ item.data.cmdlet }}</code></a>
          <p>{{ item.data.title }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cmd-card-copy">
          <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">PS&gt;</span>
          <code>{{ item.data.command }}</code>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-copy="{{ item.data.command | e }}" data-track-value="{{ item.fileSlug }}">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="more-links"><a href="/commands/">All {{ collections.commands.length }} commands</a> <a href="/cheat-sheet/">Printable cheat sheet</a></p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">The commands</p>
    <h2>Grouped the way you look them up</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    {% for cat in collections.commandCategories %}
      <a class="card card-stat" href="/commands/#{{ cat.slug }}">
        <p class="card-count">{{ cat.count }}</p>
        <h3>{{ cat.label }}</h3>
        <p>command{% if cat.count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</p>
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="kicker">Tools</p>
    <h2>When copying is not enough</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <a class="card" href="/from-bash/">
      <p class="kicker">Translate</p>
      <h3>From bash or cmd</h3>
      <p>Know <code>grep</code>, <code>ls -la</code>, or <code>ipconfig</code>? Find the PowerShell way, plus the gotchas.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/explain/">
      <p class="kicker">Explain</p>
      <h3>What does this command do?</h3>
      <p>Paste a line you found online. See each step in plain English, with warnings for anything risky.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/builders/">
      <p class="kicker">Build</p>
      <h3>Fill in the blanks</h3>
      <p>Forms that write the script for you: copy, rename, clean up, zip, schedule.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/cheat-sheet/">
      <p class="kicker">Print</p>
      <h3>One-page cheat sheet</h3>
      <p>Every command on two sides of paper. Tape it next to your monitor.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
